# Deny-by-default. `*` ignores everything; each rule below names back exactly
# what gh-widgets ships. An unlisted file is invisible to git and can never be
# committed by accident — which is the point, because this working tree also
# holds .secrecy-literals, a .venv, .worktrees/ and the rendered widgets/
# output.
#
# The mechanic, because the pattern fails silently without it: git does not
# look inside a directory it has already ignored. So every kept directory is
# re-opened (`!dir/`), its contents denied again (`dir/*`), and its files are
# named back by a glob SCOPED to that directory. That scoping is the point —
# it is what stops a `!*.py` from reaching into `__pycache__/`, `.venv/` or
# the generated `widgets/` tree.
#
# Runtime modules live in src/ and tests in tests/. Each directory below
# re-opens only its shipped file types; generated __pycache__/ trees stay
# denied by the leading `*`. The public ghwidgets_data.py boundary stays
# at the root for pinned consumers.
#
# Adding a file whose type is not already named back for its directory means
# adding a rule here. `git status` will NOT tell you the file is missing; it
# simply never appears. `git check-ignore -v <path>` names the rule hiding an
# UNTRACKED file. For a tracked file, add `--no-index`: check-ignore otherwise
# consults the index, and a tracked path is never subject to the rules.

*

# ---- repository root — public boundary, docs and project config ----------
!/ghwidgets_data.py
!/.gitignore
!/.pylintrc
!/.gitleaks.toml
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/LICENSE
!/PRESENTATION.txt
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/VERSION
!/install.sh
!/pyrightconfig.json
!/setup.cfg

# ---- src/ — renderers and their shared runtime modules --------------------
!/src/
/src/*
!/src/*.py

# ---- tests/ — stdlib unittest package ------------------------------------
!/tests/
/tests/*
!/tests/*.py

# ---- gate/ — committed coverage and speed records ------------------------
!/gate/
/gate/*
!/gate/coverage-floor.json
!/gate/speed-baseline.json

# ---- requirements/ — pinned development and CI toolchains ----------------
!/requirements/
/requirements/*
!/requirements/dev.txt
!/requirements/test.txt
!/requirements/pip-audit.txt
!/requirements/zizmor.txt

# ---- .github/ — CI workflows, dependabot, issue and PR templates ----------
!/.github/
/.github/*
!/.github/dependabot.yml
!/.github/comment-share.json
!/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
!/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/*
!/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/*.md
!/.github/workflows/
/.github/workflows/*
!/.github/workflows/*.yml

# ---- docs/ — design docs and specs -----------------------------------------
!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/*.html
!/docs/*.md
!/docs/*.txt
!/docs/superpowers/
/docs/superpowers/*
!/docs/superpowers/plans/
/docs/superpowers/plans/*
!/docs/superpowers/plans/*.html
!/docs/superpowers/plans/*.md
!/docs/superpowers/specs/
/docs/superpowers/specs/*
!/docs/superpowers/specs/*.html
!/docs/superpowers/specs/*.md

# ---- examples/ — sample unit, timer and nginx config -----------------------
!/examples/
/examples/*
!/examples/*.conf
!/examples/*.service
!/examples/*.timer

# ---- scripts/ — repo tooling ------------------------------------------------
!/scripts/
/scripts/*
!/scripts/*.py
!/scripts/*.sh
!/scripts/pre-push
!/scripts/bench/
/scripts/bench/*
!/scripts/bench/*.py
!/scripts/ci/
/scripts/ci/*
!/scripts/ci/*.py

# ---- units/ — the systemd units actually deployed ---------------------------
!/units/
/units/*
!/units/*.service
!/units/*.timer

# ---- fixtures/diff_coverage/ — offline patch-coverage inputs ---------------
!/fixtures/
/fixtures/*
!/fixtures/diff_coverage/
/fixtures/diff_coverage/*
!/fixtures/diff_coverage/*.xml
!/fixtures/diff_coverage/*.diff
